;; The GPU kernel artifact table: which SPIR-V module the guests load under
;; each name, pinned by SHA-256 (JUN-375; amu ADR 0374 option D, ADR 0371
;; Decision 9). Amu selfhost builds the modules with KIR v2. Inference does not
;; build them; it stages them by name, and its native gate checks each digest
;; against this table and against Amu's receipt.
;;
;; :amu/commit           Amu's tree that builds the modules
;; :amu/receipt,
;; :amu/receipt-sha256   a passing GPU receipt of that tree's build (RADV on
;;                       gad), which the pins equal, and the receipt file's
;;                       own digest
;;
;; :spv       the name the guests load from their SPIR-V directory (the
;;            decode guest's layout table in gen_decode_tokens_guest.cljk
;;            names ten of these; kdot_x8r8 is gen_kdot_guest's x8r8 layout)
;; :amu       the module's name in Amu's build (suite kir2)
;; :ref       Amu's glslang module of the same kernel
;; :gpu       the receipt's GPU pair: v2-<gpu> is :amu and ref-<gpu> is :ref,
;;            run and compared byte for byte on the GPU
;; :bytes,
;; :sha256    the module, equal to the receipt's entry for :amu
;; :replaces  the glslang build this module takes the place of. glslang of that
;;            source (-V --target-env vulkan1.1) is byte-identical to :ref
;;            (fetch.sh checks it on every fetch)
;;
;; One artifact per line, keys in this order: kir2_artifacts.kotoba reads the
;; table as text. ASCII only, and no comment from :artifacts to the end.
